%F A401843 a(n) = 2*n - A401844(n).
%e A401843 a(7) = 4. For all k such that 49 < k < 64, according to A003285, only 4 numbers have an odd period for the continued fraction of the square root of k, namely: 50, 53, 58, and 61.
